From 1d6cd3040ca6f9a12c2ac227ab8cd4d9a9070922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stoatium Build <stoatium@localhost>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 13:41:58 +0300
Subject: i18n(ru) + ui: complete the catalog, fix contrast and layout
 artefacts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Translations
  At this revision 564 of 800 Russian strings are untranslated, so most of
  the UI renders in English. 462 are backported verbatim from upstream's
  later v0.14.1 catalog; 101 are translated fresh.

  Four more strings were not translat*able* at all -- bare literals that
  never reach the catalog, so no amount of translating would have fixed
  them. "Direct Messages" sits in a file that already imports Trans and
  uses it two lines above; Friends.tsx passes title="Online" and friends as
  plain props; MemberSidebar interpolates "{n} members online" inline.
  These are now wrapped.

Contrast
  Two Material 3 token mispairings made text unreadable, and no contrast
  setting could fix them because the palette was fine and only the token
  reference was wrong:
    - SidebarButton set background: primary-container when selected but
      left color at on-surface, so the selected entry was white on light
      grey.
    - UserSummary paired primary-container with on-primary, which is the
      foreground for `primary`, not for its container.

Layout
  The navigation rail is a fixed 56px, sized for "Blocked"; Russian's
  "Заблокированный" overflowed and clipped. Widened to 72px and the label
  shortened to "Блокировки".

  ProfileJoined strips / and - from the locale's date format but not "."
  Russian's L format is DD.MM.YYYY and its abbreviated months carry their
  own trailing dot, which produced "02.авг..2026".

Defaults
  Accent #5865F2, contrast 0.5, variant vibrant. tonal_spot at zero
  contrast is what desaturated everything to grey. These are defaults only;
  every Appearance setting still overrides them.
